coder › Changed `src/emitter.ts` and `src/emitter.test.ts` on branch `fix/emit-snapshot` (2 commits).

What changed:
- `src/emitter.ts` — `emit` now iterates a snapshot taken when emit began (`[...(this.#listeners.get(event) ?? [])]`) instead of the live array. Every listener registered at emit start is called exactly once in registration order, whatever any of them adds/removes meanwhile; listeners added during emit wait for the next emit. This also fixes `once` (which is `off`-during-emit) silencing the listener after it. `once`/`off`/`emit` return semantics were already correct and are unchanged.
- `src/emitter.test.ts` — added 8 tests: self-removal doesn't skip next, `once`-before-ordinary doesn't silence it, earlier-listener removal still calls the removed listener that emit, add-during-emit deferred to next emit, `once` fires exactly once, `off` returns whether it removed anything, `emit` returns call count (incl. 0 for unknown event), registration order.

